{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkQuantityMarshalJSON","summary":"The benchmark now runs one sub-benchmark per quantity using b.Loop, rather than cycling values with b.N. Only benchmark structure changed.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"MarshalJSON benchmark split into per-quantity sub-benchmarks with b.Loop","confidence":0.94,"reason":"Benchmark-only restructuring in a test file with no production effect.","risk_signals":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkQuantityUnmarshalJSON","summary":"The benchmark now marshals each quantity once, then runs a per-quantity sub-benchmark that unmarshals the data with b.Loop. Only benchmark structure changed.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"UnmarshalJSON benchmark split into per-quantity sub-benchmarks","confidence":0.94,"reason":"Benchmark-only restructuring in a test file with no production effect.","risk_signals":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkCanonicalize","summary":"The benchmark now runs per-quantity sub-benchmarks with b.Loop and a per-case buffer. Only benchmark structure changed.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Canonicalize benchmark split into per-quantity sub-benchmarks","confidence":0.94,"reason":"Benchmark-only restructuring in a test file with no production effect.","risk_signals":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkQuantityRoundUp","summary":"The benchmark now runs per-quantity sub-benchmarks and uses DeepCopy instead of a shallow copy, so iterations do not share the decimal state that RoundUp mutates. The comment's claim holds for quantities with a non-nil inf.Dec.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"RoundUp benchmark uses DeepCopy per iteration in sub-benchmarks","confidence":0.92,"reason":"Benchmark-only change in a test file with no production effect.","risk_signals":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkQuantityCopy","summary":"The benchmark now runs per-quantity sub-benchmarks with b.Loop. Only benchmark structure changed.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Copy benchmark split into per-quantity sub-benchmarks","confidence":0.94,"reason":"Benchmark-only restructuring in a test file with no production effect.","risk_signals":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkQuantityAdd","summary":"The benchmark now runs per-quantity sub-benchmarks with b.Loop, resetting the base value on each iteration as before. Only benchmark structure changed.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Add benchmark split into per-quantity sub-benchmarks","confidence":0.94,"reason":"Benchmark-only restructuring in a test file with no production effect.","risk_signals":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkQuantityCmp","summary":"The benchmark now runs per-quantity sub-benchmarks with b.Loop. Only benchmark structure changed.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Cmp benchmark split into per-quantity sub-benchmarks","confidence":0.94,"reason":"Benchmark-only restructuring in a test file with no production effect.","risk_signals":[]}
]}

{"units":[
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:ParseQuantity","summary":"ParseQuantity now canonicalizes and caches the string form on the two return paths that did not already set it. Parsed quantities carry q.s from creation, so later String() calls do not need to mutate them.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"ParseQuantity now always caches the canonical string","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Changes the state of every parsed Quantity (cached s field), which affects equality comparisons, encoding and concurrency behavior.","risk_signals":["public API behavior","concurrency","extra work on every parse"],"focus":["every return path of ParseQuantity sets q.s (early returns, overflow/maxAllowed path)","callers or tests comparing parsed Quantity with reflect.DeepEqual against constructed ones","parse cost increase from canonicalizing eagerly"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:(*Quantity).String","summary":"String() no longer writes the computed string back into the receiver; it returns the cached value if present, otherwise computes it each time. This removes a data race on concurrent reads but makes String() on uncached quantities recompute every call.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"String() no longer mutates receiver and caches nothing","confidence":0.85,"reason":"Changes caching and mutation semantics of a widely used public method, with performance and concurrency consequences.","risk_signals":["public API behavior","concurrency","performance regression for non-parsed quantities"],"focus":["hot paths that build Quantity via NewQuantity/Add/etc. and call String repeatedly","code or tests relying on String() populating q.s"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity.go:(*Quantity).CacheString","summary":"Adds exported CacheString, which computes the canonical string and always stores it on the receiver. Callers must own the instance since it writes.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"behavior","headline":"Add exported Quantity.CacheString that stores canonical string","confidence":0.85,"reason":"New public API that mutates the receiver, with concurrency contract on callers.","risk_signals":["public API","mutates receiver","concurrency"],"focus":["CacheString is only called on instances not shared across goroutines","unconditional write is acceptable for callers holding shared read-only values"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:TestQuantityString","summary":"The test now expects ParseQuantity to set the cached string and drops the check that String() populates q.s. The expectation was changed to match the new String() behavior.","issues":[],"bucket":"human","change_kind":"test","headline":"TestQuantityString expects parse-time caching, drops String-caching assertion","confidence":0.7,"reason":"Expectations were changed to match new behavior and an assertion was removed, which could hide a regression.","risk_signals":["assertion removed","expectation changed"],"focus":["the removed assertion is covered by the new ParseQuantity cache check and TestQuantityCacheString"]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:TestQuantityCacheString","summary":"New test covering CacheString: it populates q.s, is idempotent, and returns <nil> for a nil receiver. It only exercises the new method.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"Add test for Quantity.CacheString","confidence":0.92,"reason":"New test only; cannot affect production behavior.","risk_signals":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkQuantityString","summary":"Benchmark rewritten to use sub-benchmarks per quantity with b.Loop, and the Precalc variant is removed. It affects only benchmarks.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"BenchmarkQuantityString restructured into per-value sub-benchmarks","confidence":0.92,"reason":"Benchmark-only change; no production effect.","risk_signals":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkQuantityStringBinarySI","summary":"Benchmark restructured into per-value sub-benchmarks using b.Loop. It affects only benchmark code.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"BenchmarkQuantityStringBinarySI restructured into sub-benchmarks","confidence":0.92,"reason":"Benchmark-only change; no production effect.","risk_signals":[]},
{"id":"staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/api/resource/quantity_test.go:BenchmarkParseQuantity","summary":"Benchmark now iterates the shared test cases as sub-benchmarks and no longer checks errors. It affects only benchmark code.","issues":[],"bucket":"skim","change_kind":"test","headline":"BenchmarkParseQuantity uses shared test cases as sub-benchmarks","confidence":0.92,"reason":"Benchmark-only change; no production effect.","risk_signals":[]}
]}

